              "descr": "Make a layout over the whole graph.  The layout does not run until you call `.run()` on it.",
              "formats": [
                {
                  "descr": "Make a layout over the whole graph.  The layout does not run until you call `.run()` on it.\n\nBuilt-ins: `grid`, `preset`, `circle`, `concentric`, `breadthfirst`, `random` and `force` (the GPU-capable spring–electric layout, round 18).  An external layout is passed **directly** rather than registered — v4 has no `cytoscape.use` and no string registry — by giving `impl`: a class or object implementing `{ run( ctx ), stop?() }` (see `layout/contract.mts` for the `LayoutContext` it receives).\n\nLifecycle events (`layoutstart`/`layoutready`/`layoutstop`) fire on the core, once per run; layout instances are not emitters.",
